{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310673,"nonce":"CdVEdKhvjTXe2ZOrMjG2SUlaE80=","title":"Pre-existing bugs ranked by magnitude. FIXED on branch fix/float-phi-boxing: #1 Sys.println(non-String), #2 Null\u003cscalar\u003e boxing/unboxing, ...","message":"All verified on `main` with minimal repros (one process each, so a crash cannot\nmask the next). Ranked by magnitude: silent wrong answers first, then crashes in\nbasic operations, then blocked designs, then leaks.\n\n    Sys.println(\"hello\")           -\u003e ok\n    Sys.println(42)                -\u003e SIGSEGV\n    Sys.println(2.0)               -\u003e SIGSEGV\n    var f:Float = 2.5; println(f)  -\u003e SIGSEGV\n    Sys.println(Std.string(42))    -\u003e ok\n    trace(42)                      -\u003e ok\n**ROOT CAUSE** (`compiler/src/stdlib/runtime_mapping.rs:1724`):\n`Sys.println(v:Dynamic)` maps to `haxe_string_println(s: *const HaxeString)`\nwith `types: \u0026[PtrVoid]`. A non-String argument is passed as a raw value and\nthen DEREFERENCED as a string pointer — `Sys.println(42)` dereferences 0x2A.\n(`haxe_sys_println()` in haxe_sys.rs takes NO argument and only prints a\nnewline; the mapping was moved off it deliberately, see the comment there.)\n**FIX**: type-directed lowering, exactly as `trace` already does\n(hir_to_mir.rs ~14950: traceInt -\u003e haxe_trace_int, traceFloat -\u003e ..., and\nhaxe_trace_string_struct for the pointer case). Convert by static type via\n`haxe_string_from_int` / `_from_float` / `_from_bool` / `haxe_std_string_ptr`,\nthen call `haxe_string_println`. NOT fixable in Sys.hx — it is an `extern class`\nand cannot carry a body.\nWhy it hides: every suite test and all of nue print via string concatenation\n(\"x=\" + v), which yields a String and takes the working path.\n\n    static function nc(x:Null\u003cInt\u003e):Int { if (x == null) return 0; return x; }\n    nc(9) -\u003e SIGSEGV     (and the ternary form crashes on main too)\nSame family as [[bugs_null_primitive_field_gep_corruption]] /\n[[bugs_null_class_field_and_onearg_cast_xmodule]].\n**WARNING**: while fixing the Float boxing I briefly turned this crash into\n`nc(9) == 0` — a SILENT WRONG ANSWER. A crash replaced by silent corruption is\nworse, not better. The guard that prevents it is \"the pointer branch must be\nliterally `HirExprKind::Null`\"; see 4ee879d8.\n\n`convert_type` says `Null\u003cInt|Float|Bool\u003e` IS a boxed `DynamicValue*`, and the\nruntime unboxers already tolerate a tagged/!null box. The representation was\nnever the problem — **the invariant was not enforced at either end**:\n  - OUT: `maybe_unbox_value` only treated `TypeKind::Dynamic` as boxed, so\n    `var y:Int = x` bitcast the box POINTER into an Int slot (printed\n    37000714080 for 9). Fixed 10e99cc6.\n  - IN: the call-site coercion was gated on `param_is_dynamic`, so a raw scalar\n    travelled into a `Ptr(U8)` slot and the callee dereferenced it. Fixed\n    b19efeff.\n**Neither half works alone.** Fixing only the caller had NO effect (the gate\nmeant maybe_box_value was never called) and fixing only the callee left the\ncrash. `null` needs no tag of its own: address 0 is unambiguous and the runtime\nalready checks `value_ptr.is_null()`.\nTOOL: when codegen panics you get no MIR dump. A probe at the LLVM compare\nprinting `operand_ty` vs the actual LLVM value kind\n(`operand_ty=Some(Ptr(U8)) left_kind=float`) is what located the gate.\n\n**MY EARLIER CHARACTERISATION WAS WRONG.** \"Adding a static to Q4Matmul breaks\ncross-module statics\" is FALSE — statics alone build fine. Bisected on the real\nnue bundle (each variant = full `rayzor bundle`, cache cleared):\n\n| variant | result |\n|---|---|\n| add `static var` + `static inline var` + static fn, NEVER CALLED | **ok** |\n| ...and CALL it, result NOT captured by the band closure | **ok** |\n| static fn with NO static var, result CAPTURED by the closure | **ok** |\n| static fn that TOUCHES A STATIC VAR, result CAPTURED by the closure | **E0100** |\n\nSo the trigger is the CONJUNCTION: a lambda capturing a value that flows out of\na function which touches a `static var`. It then breaks OTHER classes' statics —\n`E0100 Cannot access field 'dumpPlan' / 'dumpAttnProfile' / 'dumpDecodeSplit'`\n(dumpDecodeSplit is in Q4Matmul itself, the other two in GQAttention).\n\nReproduce: in `nue/nue/Q4Matmul.hx` add\n`static var _bandScratch` + `bandScratchBase(w)` that grows it, then have the\n`matmul`/`matmulFused` band closure capture `bandScratchBase(...)`'s result.\n`rayzor bundle nue/examples/llama-chat/Main.hx` then fails.\n\nSame id-space family as [[bugs_new_module_static_only_sigsegv]]. The shipped fix\n(1770a9ee) sidesteps it with a per-call buffer, which captures only a local.\n\nAfter the fixes above the profile HALVED: 9,312,982 allocs / 871 MB -\u003e\n4,447,478 / 424 MB on the same run. What is left:\n    305,290  haxe_bytes_sub_i64      (BPETokenizer:622, per decoded piece)\n    257,719  haxe_array alloc\n     41.5 MB haxe_bytes_alloc (2,274 calls -- was 1,986,849)\n**DO NOT \"optimise\" BPETokenizer:622 to `getString`.** Tried\n`combined.sub(0,k).toString()` -\u003e `combined.getString(0,k)`: it BROKE\ndetokenisation (output went essentially empty). `getString` applies UTF-8\nencoding semantics; byte-level BPE deliberately carries invalid-UTF-8\nintermediates, which is why the code takes a raw Bytes copy and `toString`s it.\nAny fix here must preserve raw byte semantics. Verify by DIFFING GENERATED TEXT,\nnot by counting allocations.\n\n`haxe_box_*` is not a tracked allocation source, and loop-body non-string/\nnon-array allocations are explicitly skipped. See\n[[reference_insert_free_actual_conditions]]. Two of the biggest consumers were\nremoved at the source (1770a9ee, 4ee879d8) rather than by fixing the pass.\n\nKeys a leaked buffer by RAW ADDRESS; a freed+reallocated weight at the same\naddress with the same length returns stale f16 data. Never called in the llama\npath (instrumented, zero hits), so it is a latent correctness hazard rather\nthan a live one.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_preexisting_ranked_2026_08_10` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}